Somebody recently posted a request for a way to permanently dispose of
unwanted objects.  Various ways to do this within Nethack 3.1.3 were
suggested but none of them really destroyed the objects, so no memory
or save-file space was saved.
Why not add recycling bins that actually destroy objects placed in
them?  There could be different bins for different materials: glass,
iron, paper/cloth/leather, plastic, etc. and maybe some rare special
ones that can take anything regardless of the material.
These bins would be just a different kind of container... very heavy,
and not lockable.  You can put things in but you can't take anything out. :-)
Anything that is put in gets deallocated.
Or perhaps you can take anything out of the bins that is in them, but
things you put in don't remain there for long.

Could you get rid of an iron ball by putting it in an iron recycling bin?
Perhaps... but it might suck you in and recycle you too!

